    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nAttractive Farm opportunity comprising a traditional renovated and extended farmhouse, farm buildings and 77 acres approximately located off the Drimoleague to Bantry road and commanding a predominantly south facing aspect.\n\nLAND: 15 acres approximately laid out in grass. The lands enjoy a sunny and sheltered aspect and are ideal for a farm enterprise.\n\nFORESTRY: 62 acres approximately of maturing forestry that is predominantly Sitka Spruce and there are some areas of native planting. The forestry is planted 15 years approximately and benefits from an ongoing premium.\n\nHOUSE: The house is a renovated and extended two-storey slated home that is finished to a comfortable standard. The accommodation includes open plan living / dining room with kitchen off, 2 bedrooms and a bathroom upstairs.\n\nSERVICES: Private water supply, electricity, septic tank and oil-fired central heating.\n\nOUTBUILDINGS: There is a traditional stone built and slated store adjacent to the house. The farmyard is located adjacent to the entrance to the property and comprises a shed and cattle house.\n\nThe property represents an opportunity to purchase a convenient property either together or in suitable lots.\n\nDisclaimer:\nWhilst every care has been taken in the preparation of these particulars, all information is provided in good faith and is believed to be correct, but is not guaranteed. Interested parties should satisfy themselves as to the accuracy and completeness of all details by independent inspection or enquiry. No representation or warranty is made regarding the condition, measurements, boundaries, planning status, services or other information relating to the property. All measurements, maps, photographs and distances are approximate and for guidance purposes only. Photographs, video and drone imagery are provided for illustrative purposes and may include features, furnishings or items not included in the sale."
      },
